Place @dried Anaheim chile peppers{5}(stemmed and seeded) and @guajillo chile peppers{5}(stemmed and seeded) in a #saucepan{}; cover with @water{to cover} and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer until tender, about ~{15%minutes}. Set aside to cool for ~{5%minutes}.

Transfer chiles and water into a #blender{}; add @onion{0.25}, @mixed spices{1%tablespoon}, and @salt{1%tablespoon}. Blend until smooth.

Place @cubed beef stew meat{3%pounds} in a large #pot{}; stir in pureed chile mixture and add @bay leaves{6}. Cook over medium-low heat until meat is very tender, ~{3-5%hours}.